<title>PORTUGAL: Yield falls on Portugal 3-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Portugal 3-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the state auction for 20 billion escudos of three-year fixed-rate bonds (OT), the Institute of Public Credit Management said.</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal	MATURITY: 23/3/99</p>
<p>    COUPON:8.5	   AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.838625</p>
<p>    AMOUNT PLACED 20 BLN ESC     AMOUNT OFFERED: 20 BLN</p>
<p>    HIGHEST ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.85 PCT    MIN YIELD: 5.80</p>
<p>DEMAND: 72.3 BLN</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 312.2 the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
